# Bifrost Schema

All tables are pre-declared `DomainTable` instances registered at boot. The physical schemas below are what DataFusion sees at scan time; they include system columns. The Rust record types in `wyrd-spec` (`SpanRecord`, `GenAiSpanRecord`, etc.) are the canonical source; this page documents the derived physical layout.

## Table namespaces

### Shared signal tables

**Namespace:** `vala.traces`, `vala.metrics`, `vala.logs`, `vala.eval`, `vala.drift`, `vala.dev`

**Partitioning:** `Day(event_time) + Bucket(tenant, 64)`

**Tenant isolation:** `data_tenant_id` column + bucket + `FilterExec` (via `TenantPredicateRule`)

All tenants write to the same physical Iceberg table. The `data_tenant_id` column + partitioning bucket enforce tenant isolation at scan time.

### Tenant-scoped dynamic datasets

**Namespace:** `vala.datasets.<tenant_uuid>.<name>`

**Partitioning:** `Day(event_time) + Bucket(tenant, 64)` (collapses to 1 slot for single-tenant tables)

**Tenant isolation:** Physical namespace + `data_tenant_id` + `FilterExec`

User-defined datasets for high-volume custom observability writes. Each tenant gets its own physical table namespace. Schema defined at Data Card registration.

## Common system columns (all tables)

| Column | Physical type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `data_tenant_id` | `Utf8` | Tenant isolation key (server-stamped) |
| `wyrd_event_time` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` | Canonical event time for partitioning and windowing |
| `wyrd_ingested_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` | Server-side flush wall clock |
| `wyrd_batch_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(16)` | Batch deduplication key |
| `run_id` | `Utf8` (nullable) | Correlation: job/experiment run |
| `card_uid` | `Utf8` (nullable) | Correlation: owning Card |
| `principal_id` | `Utf8` (nullable) | Correlation: emitting principal |

## vala.traces.spans

The sole canonical durable table for the OTLP trace signal. Its ledger lives in
`vala-bifrost-redux::tables::traces::spans::SPAN_FIELDS`; each field carries an
immutable table-local id published as `PARQUET:field_id`. Span events, span
links, resource, scope, and the promoted GenAI attributes are columns of this
table — there are no child tables.

| Column | Physical type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `trace_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(16)` | 128-bit trace ID |
| `span_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(8)` | 64-bit span ID |
| `parent_span_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(8)` nullable | Absent for root span |
| `trace_state` | `Utf8` | W3C tracestate |
| `flags` | `Int64` | OpenTelemetry span flags; Iceberg has no unsigned integer type |
| `name` | `Utf8` | Span operation name |
| `kind` | `Int32` | OTLP `SpanKind` enum value |
| `start_time_unix_nano` | `Int64` | Span start |
| `end_time_unix_nano` | `Int64` | Span end |
| `duration_nano` | `Int64` | `end_time_unix_nano - start_time_unix_nano` |
| `status_present` | `Bool` | Distinguishes an absent status from a present empty one |
| `status_code` | `Int32` nullable | |
| `status_message` | `Utf8` nullable | **payload-gated** |
| `attributes` | `Binary` | Canonical KeyValue encoding, **payload-gated** |
| `dropped_attributes_count` | `Int64` | |
| `events` | `List<Struct>` | Nested span events, **payload-gated** |
| `dropped_events_count` | `Int64` | |
| `links` | `List<Struct>` | Nested span links, **payload-gated** |
| `dropped_links_count` | `Int64` | |
| `resource_present` | `Bool` | |
| `resource_attributes` | `Binary` | **payload-gated** |
| `resource_dropped_attributes_count` | `Int64` | |
| `resource_schema_url` | `Utf8` | |
| `resource_entity_refs` | `List<Binary>` | Pinned `EntityRef` encoding, **payload-gated** |
| `scope_present` | `Bool` | |
| `scope_name` | `Utf8` | |
| `scope_version` | `Utf8` | |
| `scope_attributes` | `Binary` | **payload-gated** |
| `scope_dropped_attributes_count` | `Int64` | |
| `scope_schema_url` | `Utf8` | |
| `service_name` | `Utf8` nullable | Promoted from resource attributes |
| `gen_ai_operation_name` | `Utf8` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_provider_name` | `Utf8` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_request_model` | `Utf8` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_conversation_id` | `Utf8` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_usage_input_tokens` | `Int64` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_usage_output_tokens` | `Int64` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| + system columns | | |

Nested `events` elements carry `time_unix_nano`, `name`, `attributes`, and
`dropped_attributes_count`. Nested `links` elements carry `trace_id`,
`span_id`, `trace_state`, `flags`, `attributes`, and
`dropped_attributes_count`. Both subtrees are entirely caller content and are
omitted by a metadata-only projection.

